{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nRepo-root scratch (`<repo>/bridge_state/`) is written by `fetcher.py:606,615`, `applier.py:555,664`, `apply_planning.py:341`, `load_phase.py:159,179,183`, `alert_store.py:20-23,100`, `dispatch_one.py:113,165`, `apply_inbound.py:107`, `apply_handlers.py:584`, `invariants.py:351-371`, with prose in `persist_phase.py:162`, `sync_logger.py:8` and `binding_repository.py:9`; it grows unbounded, sits at the repo root (bug `germinable-cosey-vireo` symptom), and `reconcile.py:132` falsely documents the prev snapshot there (it is `<tracker>/.bridge_state/prev_snapshot.json`, `load_phase.py:210-212`). `.gitignore:23` `.rebar/*` ignores everything under `.rebar/` with surgical un-ignores (`:24-`), so `.rebar/bridge/` needs no new pattern and `.gitignore:14` `bridge_state/` becomes dead. `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py` uses the git file list (bug `germinable-cosey-vireo`, closed); only its comment `:28` names `bridge_state/`. Tracker-side `<tracker>/.bridge_state/` (bindings, projects, prev_snapshot, last-pass) is committed state and is not renamed. Cites are on origin/main 031be25ced9.\n\n## Approach\n1. New `src/rebar/reconciler/scratch_retention.py` (~120 LOC): `BRIDGE_SCRATCH_SUBDIR = Path(\".rebar\")/\"bridge\"`, `bridge_scratch_dir(repo_root)`, `snapshots_dir()`, `alerts_dir()`, `sync_log_path(repo_root, pass_id)`, `mapping_path()`, `divergence_state_path()`, constants `RETAIN_SNAPSHOT_PASSES = 5`, `RETAIN_SYNC_LOGS = 5`, `RETAIN_ALERT_DAYS = 30`, and `prune_bridge_scratch(repo_root, *, keep_passes=…, keep_logs=…, keep_alert_days=…) -> dict[str, int]` — best-effort, exception-swallowing (`logger.warning`), mirroring `llm/completion_sidecar.py:46,248-275` (`RETAIN_PER_TICKET`, `prune(keep=…)`): snapshots grouped by pass-id prefix (`<pass>.json`, `<pass>.manifest.json`, stray `<pass>.*.json.tmp`), newest-by-name (pass ids are `%Y-%m-%dT%H-%M-%S`, lexically ordered); `sync-log-*.jsonl` by name; `bridge_alerts/YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl` keeps the 30 newest files. `mapping.json` and `comment_id_divergence.json` are cross-pass state and are never pruned.\n2. Every writer module imports these path helpers (`alert_store._STATE_SUBDIR` deleted).\n3. Call `prune_bridge_scratch(ctx.repo_root)` in `persist_phase.persist_and_log` after `sync_logger.close()` (`:251`), guarded by `if persist:`.\n4. Fix `reconcile.py:132`; `docs/adr/0099-binding-store-internal-ownership.md:72` row → `<repo_root>/.rebar/bridge/bridge_alerts/*.jsonl`; delete `.gitignore:14`; update the `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:28` comment; fix the prose in `persist_phase.py`, `sync_logger.py` and `binding_repository.py`; add the BREAKING entries to `CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/release-notes.md`. `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` and `docs/concurrency.md` name only the tracker-side `.bridge_state/` (committed state, not renamed), so they need no change.\n5. Tests: the 53 files outside `tests/fixtures/` matched by `git grep -lE '(^|[^._A-Za-z])bridge_state' origin/main -- tests` re-spell the path via the helpers, excluding `tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py` (stays as-is); frozen `tests/fixtures/` corpora are not edited. New `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_scratch_retention.py`. No migration of existing `bridge_state/` dirs (scratch; operators delete it).\n\nBREAKING: reconciler scratch moves from `<repo>/bridge_state/` to `<repo>/.rebar/bridge/`; snapshots and sync logs keep the last 5 passes, alerts the last 30 days.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/reconciler/scratch_retention.py` (new), the nine writer modules `src/rebar/reconciler/{alert_store,fetcher,applier,apply_planning,load_phase,dispatch_one,apply_inbound,apply_handlers,invariants}.py`, `src/rebar/reconciler/{persist_phase,reconcile,sync_logger,binding_repository}.py`, `.gitignore`, `docs/adr/0099-binding-store-internal-ownership.md:72`, `docs/release-notes.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:28`, the tests named above. Out of scope: tracker-side `<tracker>/.bridge_state/` (committed state, not renamed), any new `.gitignore` pattern, and migration of existing scratch dirs.\n\n## Testing\nHappy: `pytest tests/unit/reconciler/state tests/unit/reconciler/fetch tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate -q`; a live-mode `reconcile_once` in a tmp repo writes under `<root>/.rebar/bridge/` and nothing under `<root>/bridge_state/`. Edge (new `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_scratch_retention.py`): seed 7 pass ids × (`.json` + `.manifest.json`) + 7 sync logs + 35 alert days → prune leaves 5/5/30 newest and returns `{\"snapshots\": 4, \"sync_logs\": 2, \"alerts\": 5}`; unreadable dir → returns zeros, no raise; a preview pass (`persist=False`) does not prune; `git status --porcelain` after a pass shows no untracked `.rebar/bridge` (covered by `.rebar/*`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `git grep -nE '(^|[^._A-Za-z])bridge_state' -- src/rebar/reconciler scripts .gitignore` is empty — grep (`src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_drift.py`'s `bridge_state` is a local variable naming the tracker-side `.bridge_state/`).\n- [ ] Retention test passes with the exact counts above — `pytest tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_scratch_retention.py -q`.\n- [ ] `reconcile.py` docstring names `<tracker>/.bridge_state/prev_snapshot.json` — grep.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0; `make lint` exits 0 in a checkout that has run a live pass (vocabulary guard unaffected)."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792620847573961001,"uuid":"6af39c1c-d597-4837-986a-52f2650eccb2"}